<title>SWEDEN: SCA to take 250 mln skr Q4 lease surplus.</title>
<headline>SCA to take 250 mln skr Q4 lease surplus.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish forestry group SCA said on Thursday it would undertake a lease-out/lease-in deal on two LWC paper machines at its Swedish Ortviken mill, a move it said would provide a net surplus of 250 million crowns.</p>
<p>SCA said in a statement that leasing revenues and leasing expenses had been paid in advance, and the net surplus of around 250 million crowns would be reported as income from financial operations for the fourth quarter of this year.</p>
<p>The counterparties were two American banks, it said, although it did not specify which.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom, +46-8-700 1006</p>
</text>
